    "q-88507": {
      "dom_id": "step-q88507",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Plot the graph of $x=-{y}^{2}-3y.$",
      "worked_solution": "To plot $x=-{y}^{2}-3y,$ we will first plot the function $y=-{x}^{2}-3x$ and then reflect it over the line $y=x.$\n\nThe curve $y=-{x}^{2}-3x$ is a parabola. It has the following factored form:\n\n$$\ny=-x(x+3)\n$$\n\nFrom the factored form above, we get the following graph:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14240562/assets/bad18b9ff4c0dc985adcaf29cdbe0a8f41a141527060eca6c7ade5f6c05b87ea.png)\n\nNow, to get the curve $x=-{y}^{2}-3y,$ we just have to reflect the curve $y=-{x}^{2}-3x$ over the line $y=x,$ as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14240562/assets/e44da9125a68d85916bdab3f9b7a6cd10a4d812c5fb12cb9825f6e229b1655b4.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
