    "q-88514": {
      "dom_id": "step-q88514",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Plot the graph of $x=-9{y}^{2}+7y.$",
      "worked_solution": "To plot $x=-9{y}^{2}+7y,$ we will first plot the function $y=-9{x}^{2}+7x$ and then reflect it over the line $y=x.$\n\nThe curve $y=-9{x}^{2}+7x$ is a parabola. It has the following factored form:\n\n$$\ny=-x(9x-7)\n$$\n\nFrom the factored form above, we get the following graph:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14240562/assets/a8781c2736aeb53a49c4f7627fb5262f1c3ef90162edf4e52251f86323e2e611.png)\n\nNow, to get the curve $x=-9{y}^{2}+7y,$ we just have to reflect the curve $y=-9{x}^{2}+7x$ over the line $y=x,$ as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14240562/assets/344f13842043f5eb5e0db0db694cbc5801373fe36cfc81e9324e8d02fcba5ebb.png)",
